.TH SIGACTION 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
sigaction \- install or inspect a signal action
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <signal.h>
.B int sigaction(int signal, const struct sigaction* action, struct sigaction* previous);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Installs action when non\-NULL and writes the previous action when previous
is non\-NULL. The handler may be SIG_DFL, SIG_IGN, or a function.
The structure and eight\-byte sigset_t use the Linux x86\-64 kernel layout,
not the libc ABI. Supported flags include SA_RESTART, SA_NODEFER and
SA_RESETHAND. The runtime supplies its own signal\-return trampoline;
do not unload it while its handlers are installed. Queried actions may
expose the kernel restorer flag and pointer. SIG_IGN invokes a runtime helper
and is not an integer constant expression.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sigemptyset (3crunch),
.BR kill (3crunch),
.BR sigaction (2)
